{
  "caseId": "averitec-dev-0044",
  "atoms": [
    {
      "id": "atom-1",
      "text": "Deliberately infecting children to COVID-19 at “pox parties” could be a good way to help create herd immunity against COVID-19 without a vaccine.",
      "sourceText": "Deliberately infecting children to COVID-19 at “pox parties” could be a good way to help create herd immunity against COVID-19 without a vaccine.",
      "start": 0,
      "end": 145
    }
  ],
  "evidence": [
    {
      "atomId": "atom-1",
      "spans": [
        {
          "id": "doc-f72194b71ba6::sentence-7",
          "documentId": "doc-f72194b71ba6",
          "text": "Children, including very young children, can develop COVID-19. ",
          "start": 561,
          "end": 624
        },
        {
          "id": "doc-b359fc5770e9::sentence-2",
          "documentId": "doc-b359fc5770e9",
          "text": "In the past, some parents participated in “chickenpox parties” to intentionally expose their unvaccinated children to a child with chickenpox in hopes that they would get the disease. ",
          "start": 13,
          "end": 197
        },
        {
          "id": "doc-f72194b71ba6::sentence-92",
          "documentId": "doc-f72194b71ba6",
          "text": "In a situation where there is no choice — such as if the grandparent lives with the grandchildren — then the family should do everything they can to try to limit the risk of COVID-19. ",
          "start": 9104,
          "end": 9288
        },
        {
          "id": "doc-f72194b71ba6::sentence-34",
          "documentId": "doc-f72194b71ba6",
          "text": "Most children who become infected with the COVID-19 virus have no symptoms, or they have milder symptoms such as low-grade fever, fatigue, and cough. ",
          "start": 2467,
          "end": 2617
        },
        {
          "id": "doc-b359fc5770e9::sentence-15",
          "documentId": "doc-b359fc5770e9",
          "text": "Vaccinated people who get chickenpox may develop lesions that do not crust. ",
          "start": 1295,
          "end": 1371
        },
        {
          "id": "doc-b359fc5770e9::sentence-7",
          "documentId": "doc-b359fc5770e9",
          "text": "The best way to protect infants and children against chickenpox is to get them vaccinated.\n",
          "start": 537,
          "end": 628
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
